{"change_summary":"Removed the unused public `temp_repro_factor_pub` wrapper from `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs`, keeping the temperature reproduction helper internal and eliminating the dead public API surface without changing runtime behavior.","outstanding_risks":["Validation was scoped to the `tank_core` package; I did not rerun a full workspace-wide test suite.","`cargo clippy -p tank_core --tests -- -D warnings` still fails on pre-existing unrelated test-target lint issues in `crates/tank_core/tests/source_water_carbonate.rs` and `crates/tank_core/tests/molt_mineral_budget.rs`."],"steps":[{"description":"Inspect `shrimp.rs` and workspace usages to confirm whether `temp_repro_factor_pub` was real API or dead test-access scaffolding.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Remove the unused public wrapper and leave `temp_repro_factor` as the internal helper used by reproduction-readiness logic.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Run targeted and package-level validation to confirm the API cleanup does not change reproduction behavior or break `tank_core` builds.","order":3,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`rg -n \"temp_repro_factor_pub\" -S .` returned no matches after the edit.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test reproduction_factors -- --nocapture` passed (13/13).","`cargo test -p tank_core` passed across the full `tank_core` package test suite.","`cargo clippy -p tank_core -- -D warnings` passed."]}